The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
// Hardcoded retry policy for ZooKeeper connections
retryPolicy = new ExponentialBackoffRetry(1000, 3);

// Exclusion of security tests from execution
@Ignore("Security tests are excluded")
```
Reason:
The hardcoded retry policy leads to conflicts in handling secure and non-secure ZooKeeper connections due to their different authentication requirements. Additionally, excluding security tests prevents them from being executed, resulting in untested scenarios that can lead to authentication issues when both test types are run together.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
// Implementing a configurable retry policy
retryPolicy = new ExponentialBackoffRetry(1000, maxRetries);

// Removing exclusion for security tests
@Category(SecurityTests.class)
```
Reason:
The configurable retry policy allows handling different authentication mechanisms properly, avoiding conflicts when secure and non-secure tests are executed together. Furthermore, removing the exclusion for security tests ensures that they are run and validated within the testing framework, preventing potential authentication issues.

